{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1452910-custom-conditions","id":1452910,"title":"Custom Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-19T14:49:21-07:00","id":1452910,"title":"Custom Conditions","content":"Apologies if this has been done before.<br /> <br /> What are some Conditions that you have created?<br /> I'm looking for more general ones, not Conditions made for very specific fanmade material like new Bloodlines or powers, or fanmade splats.<br /> <br /> I'll start sharing my own:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">- Charming</span></b><br /> <br /> Your character has successfully charmed someone, through seduction, con artistry or convincing arguments. That person is now vulnerable to your manipulation.<br /> You may have multiple instances of this Condition, one for each target of your character's persuasion.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: you gain this Condition whenever you inflict the Swooned Condition on someone.<br /> You gain +2 to Social rolls towards the Swooned character, and increase the impression level of that person in Social Maneuvers. You can shed this Condition to automatically open one Door.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution</b>: shed this Condition and open a Door as described; take advantage of the person's vulnerability; lose the person's trust or burn bridges with her.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible sources</b>: exceptional success on a Persuasion roll<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: I think it's best to frame rewards for exceptional successes as positive Conditions to the players than giving Conditions to NPCs, so I simply adapted Swooned from the charmer's point of view.</i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">- Misinformed</span></b><br /> <br /> Your character has obtained wrong or inaccurate information about a topic.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: choose a topic upon taking this Condition. When you make a roll pertaining to that topic, you may choose to resolve this Condition. If you do, automatically fail the roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution</b>: face proof that your information is false, or resolve the Condition as described.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible sources</b>: being lied to; dramatic failure on an investigation roll.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: This can be used as an alternative to Tainted Clues when not using the Investigation rules.</i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">- New Trick</span></b><br /> <br /> Your character has learned something new on how to use her skills effectively.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: this Condition is associated with a particular action, context or use for a Skill.<br /> The next time your character performs that action, you can shed this Condition to gain +2 to the roll. If the roll succeeds, you regain 1 Willpower point.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution</b>: perform the action and shed this Condition as described.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible sources</b>: exceptional success; practice with a teacher.<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: Generic positive Condition to reward exceptional successes, as an alternative to Inspired, which I'm not fond of.</i><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">- Tasked</span></b><br /> <br /> Your character has been tasked with a duty by a superior, family, organization or bargain. <br /> The obligation on your part is probably minor, like an easy task or routine work, but letting it lapse would disappoint the person who gave the task.<br /> <br /> <b>Effect</b>: completing the task requires a few hours and could interfere with other pressing matters. You may shed this Condition to consider the task completed.<br /> Only gain a Beat if doing so causes complications to you or your group: e.g. you cannot participate to an important scene, or the hours spent put in a time pressure.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution</b>: complete the task with consequences as described, or renounce to completing the task, thus disappointing the person who gave it.<br /> <br /> <b>Possible sources</b>: a superior, an Ally, a promise, a service made as payment<br /> <br /> <i>Comments: I think this Condition handles well, in a more fluid way, a whole range of scenes that wouldn't be very interesting to play out, allowing at the same time players to add more conflict and drama.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}